PPrrooffiillee CCoommmmaannddss
     A _p_r_o_f_i_l_e file named on the command line is read one `~'
     command per line, using the same letters as the in-session
     commands ff, hh, ll, and ss above, to set the duplex, line, and
     speed before the port is opened.  A profile line beginning
     with ~ww tells ccuu to stop reading the profile and open the
     port; the remainder of the profile is then pushed back to be
     read as further `~' commands once the connection is up.

FFIILLEESS
          /ddeevv/mmooddeemm      default serial line
          /eettcc/ccuuxxccvvrr     file-transfer helper invoked by ~g and ~p

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
